    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that owner responses include a `displayName` field formatted exactly as `\"LastName, FirstName\"` from the stored names.\n\n**1. API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 Added a `displayName` read-only property to the `Owner` schema. Since DTOs are generated from this spec by the openapi-generator plugin at build time, this produces the `displayName` field on the generated `OwnerDto`. I placed it on the `Owner` schema (not `OwnerFields`) and marked it `readOnly`, so it's a computed output field and never accepted as input.\n\n**2. Mapping logic** (`OwnerMapper.java`) \u2014 Added the formatting in the DTO-mapping layer, where presentation concerns belong, keeping the domain model untouched:\n\n```java\n@Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(formatDisplayName(owner))\")\nOwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n\ndefault String formatDisplayName(Owner owner) {\n    if (owner == null) {\n        return null;\n    }\n    return owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName();\n}\n```\n\nBecause every read path (`getOwner`, `listOwners`, page listing, and the create response) routes through `toOwnerDto`, they all get `displayName` consistently with no duplicated logic.\n\n**Verification:** `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
